---
import SEOHead from '../../../components/SEOHead.astro';
import GameNav from '../../../components/GameNav.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import SideAd from '../../../components/SideAd.astro';
import InContentAd from '../../../components/InContentAd.astro';
import LevelSelector from '../../../components/LevelSelector.astro';

const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 24 Walkthrough: Hallway";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 24 walkthrough for the Hallway, the last room of Murder Dressed in White: the lock pick and the nail, the wall safe holding the Cube and the D=7 slip, the sliding-block board, the four-drum lock that gives you the Hammer, the painting and the R=5 slip, the five watches, the N=3 door, and the final keypad code 51378 — R, A, N, D and Y read as numbers. Reward and time included.";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What is the code for the last door in Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 24 Hallway?",
    a: "The five-digit code is <b>51378</b>. It is not a random number: the room hands you five letter-to-digit slips and one letter painted on a door, and each letter of the answer maps to a digit. <b>R=5</b>, <b>A=1</b>, <b>N=3</b>, <b>D=7</b>, <b>Y=8</b> in that order gives <b>5 1 3 7 8</b>. The display reads 51378 at 5:00, one frame before the lock releases, and the letter set was read twice off the inventory at 4:20. The two agreeing with each other is the real check.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where do the five letter clues come from?",
    a: "<b>D=7</b> is inside the wall safe behind the hanging coat, next to the Cube. <b>R=5</b> comes from the painting propped askew against the back wall, once you have the hammer and nail. <b>Y=8</b> is in a drawer that opens after the four-drum lock is worked, around 4:08. <b>A=1</b> is in the inventory by 4:12 but the recording does not show a clean pickup for it, so its exact source is the one thing on this page we could not pin down. <b>N=3</b> is not a slip at all — it is painted on the wooden door panel at 4:18.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why 51378 and not 73155 or any other order?",
    a: "Because the numbers spell the word. Read the five letters that have digits attached — R, A, N, D, Y — left to right as they appear in the inventory, substitute each digit, and you get 5-1-3-7-8. Any other permutation produces a number that matches no word in the room. That self-consistency is also the cross-check: the digits we read off the keypad display are exactly the digits those five letters carry.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I open the wall safe in the Hallway?",
    a: "Two steps. First use the lock pick — it is the item card at 0:14 — on the wall lock at 0:21 and work the pin-tumbler mini-game until the drawer pops. That gives you a <b>Nail</b>. Then move the coat hanging on the coat-rack unit: a two-dial wall safe is behind it at 0:30. The <b>Key</b> in your inventory opens it, and the safe holds the blue <b>Cube</b> and the <b>D=7</b> slip.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the Cube for?",
    a: "The sliding-block board. The board is a four-by-four grid with a fixed purple padlock tile, a movable green key tile and two light-blue X blocker tiles. The Cube is the piece the board is missing. Your job is to slide the green key tile through the free cells until it lands on the padlock; the board closes at 2:18. It is pure sliding-block logic, no numbers involved.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where is the Hammer and how do I get it?",
    a: "The wooden box sitting on top of the shoe rack on the far left wall has a four-drum combination lock — three digits visible per drum, the middle row being the active one. Roll the drums and the lid opens at 3:07, and the <b>Hammer</b> card follows at 3:09. You then combine it with the Nail: the inventory shows a single <b>Hammer and nail</b> card at 3:15.",
  },
  {
    q: "What do I do with the hammer and nail?",
    a: "Use them on the landscape painting hanging askew against the back wall, right of the dresser. The close-up at 3:19 shows the painting with a torn strip of paper trapped under the bottom of the frame. Once the frame is levered, the <b>R=5</b> slip comes free at 3:24.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the answer to the five watches?",
    a: "The watches read <b>09:05</b>, <b>08:53</b>, <b>08:29</b>, <b>07:53</b> and a fifth showing <b>?</b>. The gap between them grows by twelve minutes each time: <b>−12</b>, <b>−24</b>, <b>−36</b>, so the next step is <b>−48</b>, which puts the fifth watch at <b>07:05</b>. The four printed times were read twice, from the full frame and from a 3x crop; the 07:05 answer is arithmetic on those reads, not something the game shows.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the four-drum lock in the Hallway?",
    a: "A metal plate with four rotating digit drums mounted into a dark wooden surface, each drum showing the digit above, the active digit in the middle and the digit below. It appears at rest showing 1 / 0 / 9 down every column, so the active row starts at <b>000</b>. The recording works it twice — once on the shoe-rack box for the Hammer, and again around 4:05, after which a drawer opens on the <b>Y=8</b> slip. The middle row at that moment reads <b>0 7 8 4</b>.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where is the N=3 clue?",
    a: "Painted on the wooden door panel below the stairs, on the same wall as the electronic keypad. The camera holds on it at <b>4:18</b> and again at 4:29; the marking is a scratched white <b>N=3</b> on dark wood. It is the only one of the five letters that is not a paper slip.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is Hallway the last level of Chapter 3?",
    a: "Yes. Chapter 3 is <i>Murder Dressed in White</i> and Hallway is <b>24 of 24</b>, the room that closes the chapter. There is a Chapter 4 in the game — <i>Pharaoh's Bride</i> — and the Hallway's exit is what leads into it. We have not written Chapter 4 guides yet, so the next-room link on this page goes back to the walkthrough hub instead.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does the recording show the level being completed?",
    a: "Yes. The keypad accepts the code at 5:00, the door opens, and the <b>LEVEL COMPLETED!</b> card lands at 5:05 with a level reward of <b>+50</b> coins and a recorded <b>Time: 5:23</b>. The piggy-bank panel sits underneath it as usual.",
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, "") },
  })),
};
