    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four honest gaps.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. Where the A=1 slip is picked up.</b> The slip is definitely in the backpack — the inventory at 4:12 and 4:20 both show <b>A=1</b> in the row with D=7, R=5 and Y=8 — but the recording never holds a clean pickup frame for it. The camera moves from the drawer to a storage alcove and back, and the slip is simply there afterwards. Its source is the one clue on this page we cannot point at.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The accepted combination on the four-drum lock.</b> The drums never stop moving in the frames we sampled. The middle row reads <b>0 7 8 4</b> at 4:05, right before the drawer opens at 4:07, so 0784 is the obvious candidate — but that is one read at one instant, not two agreeing reads, so it is printed here as a candidate rather than a code. The Hammer route at 3:07 has the same problem, which is why neither is presented as "the answer".
      <br><br>
      <b>3. What the watch answer unlocks.</b> 07:05 is solid arithmetic on four twice-read times, but the recording does not show a lock that takes a time. Either it feeds a puzzle we could not tie to a visible lock, or it is a hint for a step the run skipped. The arithmetic is offered as arithmetic, not as a verified in-game input.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The scissors and the boots.</b> Both get full close-ups and both are real pickups, but neither is visibly spent anywhere in the run. They may belong to branches the recording skipped; they are not presented here as required steps.
    </div>
